window.storyContent={"us1":"<section class=\"story-header\" id=\"us1-summary\"><h2><span id=\"src-0145\" data-source=\"SRC-0145\">Story 1 — Access the Find a Cruise component</span></h2><p class=\"story-callout\"><span id=\"src-0147\" data-source=\"SRC-0147\">As a consumer, I want to see the Find a Cruise component on the Home Page, so that I can begin searching for a cruise without navigating to another page.</span></p><p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> None · foundation for US2–US5</p><p><strong>Scope:</strong> Home Page component; illustrative data and existing design-system assumptions.</p></section><section id=\"us1-value\"><h2>Why it matters</h2><p class=\"story-callout\">Consumers can begin a cruise search from the Home Page, with no extra navigation step.</p></section><section id=\"us1-criteria\"><h2><span id=\"src-0148\" data-source=\"SRC-0148\">Acceptance criteria</span></h2><article class=\"criterion\" id=\"us1-ac1\"><div class=\"criterion-heading criterion-meta\"><span class=\"badge proposal\">US1 · AC1</span><a href=\"#us1-ac1\" aria-label=\"Link to US1 AC1\">#</a></div><h3><span id=\"src-0149\" data-source=\"SRC-0149\">AC1 — Display the component</span></h3><p class=\"scenario\"><span id=\"src-0150\" data-source=\"SRC-0150\">Scenario: Display the Find a Cruise component</span></p><p class=\"gherkin given\"><span id=\"src-0151\" data-source=\"SRC-0151\">Given the consumer navigates to the Royal Caribbean Home Page</span></p><p class=\"gherkin when\"><span id=\"src-0152\" data-source=\"SRC-0152\">When the page loads successfully</span></p><p class=\"gherkin then\"><span id=\"src-0153\" data-source=\"SRC-0153\">Then the Find a Cruise component is displayed</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0154\" data-source=\"SRC-0154\">And its placement follows the approved Home Page design</span></p></article><article class=\"criterion\" id=\"us1-ac2\"><div class=\"criterion-heading criterion-meta\"><span class=\"badge proposal\">US1 · AC2</span><a href=\"#us1-ac2\" aria-label=\"Link to US1 AC2\">#</a></div><h3><span id=\"src-0155\" data-source=\"SRC-0155\">AC2 — Display the initial filter states</span></h3><p class=\"scenario\"><span id=\"src-0156\" data-source=\"SRC-0156\">Scenario: Display the component without selected filters</span></p><p class=\"gherkin given\"><span id=\"src-0157\" data-source=\"SRC-0157\">Given the consumer opens the Home Page</span></p><p class=\"gherkin when\"><span id=\"src-0158\" data-source=\"SRC-0158\">When the Find a Cruise component is displayed</span></p><p class=\"gherkin then\"><span id=\"src-0159\" data-source=\"SRC-0159\">Then the Destination filter displays \"Any Destination\"</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0160\" data-source=\"SRC-0160\">And the Departure Port filter displays \"Any Departure Port\"</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0161\" data-source=\"SRC-0161\">And the Departure Date filter displays \"Any Date\"</span></p></article><article class=\"criterion\" id=\"us1-ac3\"><div class=\"criterion-heading criterion-meta\"><span class=\"badge proposal\">US1 · AC3</span><a href=\"#us1-ac3\" aria-label=\"Link to US1 AC3\">#</a></div><h3><span id=\"src-0162\" data-source=\"SRC-0162\">AC3 — Display the required controls</span></h3><p><span id=\"src-0163\" data-source=\"SRC-0163\">The component includes:</span></p><p class=\"bullet clean-bullet\"><span id=\"src-0164\" data-source=\"SRC-0164\">* A Destination control identified by Cruising To.</span></p><p class=\"bullet clean-bullet\"><span id=\"src-0165\" data-source=\"SRC-0165\">* A Departure Port control identified by Departing From.</span></p><p class=\"bullet clean-bullet\"><span id=\"src-0166\" data-source=\"SRC-0166\">* A Departure Date control identified by Leaving.</span></p><p class=\"bullet clean-bullet\"><span id=\"src-0167\" data-source=\"SRC-0167\">* The calendar affordance shown in Visual Reference 2.</span></p><p class=\"bullet clean-bullet\"><span id=\"src-0168\" data-source=\"SRC-0168\">* A primary action labeled Search Cruises.</span></p></article><article class=\"criterion\" id=\"us1-ac4\"><div class=\"criterion-heading criterion-meta\"><span class=\"badge proposal\">US1 · AC4</span><a href=\"#us1-ac4\" aria-label=\"Link to US1 AC4\">#</a></div><h3><span id=\"src-0169\" data-source=\"SRC-0169\">AC4 — Interpret default values as unrestricted criteria</span></h3><p class=\"scenario\"><span id=\"src-0170\" data-source=\"SRC-0170\">Scenario: Display an unrestricted initial search state</span></p><p class=\"gherkin given\"><span id=\"src-0171\" data-source=\"SRC-0171\">Given the consumer has not interacted with any filter</span></p><p class=\"gherkin then\"><span id=\"src-0172\" data-source=\"SRC-0172\">Then no destination restriction is active</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0173\" data-source=\"SRC-0173\">And no departure port restriction is active</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0174\" data-source=\"SRC-0174\">And no departure date restriction is active</span></p></article></section><section id=\"us1-references\"><h2>Visual references</h2><figure><a href=\"../assets/reference-images/01-home-page-placement.png\" aria-label=\"Expand reference image 1\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"../assets/reference-images/01-home-page-placement.png\" alt=\"Image 1: Find a Cruise component added to the Home Page\"></a><figcaption><span id=\"src-0181\" data-source=\"SRC-0181\">Image 1: Find a Cruise component added to the Home Page</span><small>Source: supplied assessment · reference 1. Activate the image for the full-size view; use Back to return.</small></figcaption></figure><figure><a href=\"../assets/reference-images/02-component-default-state.png\" aria-label=\"Expand reference image 2\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"../assets/reference-images/02-component-default-state.png\" alt=\"Image 2: Find A Cruise component loaded by default\"></a><figcaption><span id=\"src-0188\" data-source=\"SRC-0188\">Image 2: Find A Cruise component loaded by default</span><small>Source: supplied assessment · reference 2. Activate the image for the full-size view; use Back to return.</small></figcaption></figure></section><section id=\"us1-decisions\"><h2>Decisions &amp; open questions</h2><p>Temporary assumptions are not confirmed answers. Blocking decisions must be resolved before production Engineering.</p><h3><span id=\"src-0191\" data-source=\"SRC-0191\">Blocking questions and notes</span></h3><article class=\"question blocking\" id=\"us1-q1\"><span class=\"badge blocking-status\">Blocking</span> <span class=\"badge decision-status open\" aria-label=\"Open — awaiting owner confirmation\">Open</span><h4><span id=\"src-0196\" data-source=\"SRC-0196\">Are the supplied visual references approved designs or illustrative examples?</span></h4><dl><div><dt>Decision owner / domain</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0197\" data-source=\"SRC-0197\">Product Owner / UX Designer</span></dd></div><div><dt>Temporary assumption</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0198\" data-source=\"SRC-0198\">The references define the required layout, hierarchy and interaction states. Exact styling follows the Royal Caribbean design system.</span></dd></div><div><dt>Source reasoning</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0199\" data-source=\"SRC-0199\">The team needs a clear design authority against which to validate the component.</span></dd></div></dl></article><h3><span id=\"src-0200\" data-source=\"SRC-0200\">Non-blocking questions and notes</span></h3><article class=\"question \" id=\"us1-q2\"><span class=\"badge nonblocking-status\">Non-blocking</span> <span class=\"badge decision-status open\" aria-label=\"Open — awaiting owner confirmation\">Open</span><h4><span id=\"src-0205\" data-source=\"SRC-0205\">What responsive behavior is expected?</span></h4><dl><div><dt>Decision owner / domain</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0206\" data-source=\"SRC-0206\">Product Owner / UX Designer</span></dd></div><div><dt>Temporary assumption</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0207\" data-source=\"SRC-0207\">Desktop follows the supplied references. Smaller viewports adapt using the existing responsive design system.</span></dd></div><div><dt>Source reasoning</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0208\" data-source=\"SRC-0208\">Only desktop references were provided.</span></dd></div></dl></article><article class=\"question \" id=\"us1-q3\"><span class=\"badge nonblocking-status\">Non-blocking</span> <span class=\"badge decision-status open\" aria-label=\"Open — awaiting owner confirmation\">Open</span><h4><span id=\"src-0209\" data-source=\"SRC-0209\">Which accessibility and browser standards apply?</span></h4><dl><div><dt>Decision owner / domain</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0210\" data-source=\"SRC-0210\">Technical Lead / UX Designer / QA Lead</span></dd></div><div><dt>Temporary assumption</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0211\" data-source=\"SRC-0211\">The component inherits the website’s existing accessibility and browser-support standards.</span></dd></div><div><dt>Source reasoning</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0212\" data-source=\"SRC-0212\">A separate compatibility policy should not be created for this component.</span></dd></div></dl></article><h3><span id=\"src-0177\" data-source=\"SRC-0177\">Applicable quality standards — temporary assumption</span></h3><p><span id=\"src-0178\" data-source=\"SRC-0178\">The component follows the Royal Caribbean website’s existing accessibility, responsive-design and supported-browser standards.</span></p><p class=\"muted\">If an answer changes, review the affected acceptance criteria, interaction states and tests before implementation.</p></section><section id=\"us1-states\"><h2>State transitions</h2><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Current state</th><th scope=\"col\">Consumer action</th><th scope=\"col\">Resulting state</th><th scope=\"col\">Expected visible behavior</th><th scope=\"col\">Related AC</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Initial load</td><td>Open the Home Page</td><td>All panels closed</td><td>Destination, port and date unrestricted; no validation or outcome.</td><td>US1 AC1–AC2</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section id=\"us1-traceability\"><h2>Traceability</h2><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">ID</th><th scope=\"col\">Source requirement</th><th scope=\"col\">Covered by</th><th scope=\"col\">Acceptance evidence</th><th scope=\"col\">Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label=\"ID\">REQ-01</td><td data-label=\"Source requirement\">Display the component on the Home Page.</td><td data-label=\"Covered by\">US1</td><td data-label=\"Acceptance evidence\">US1 AC1</td><td data-label=\"Status\">Covered</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"ID\">REQ-02</td><td data-label=\"Source requirement\">Display three filters with generic initial values.</td><td data-label=\"Covered by\">US1</td><td data-label=\"Acceptance evidence\">US1 AC2–AC4</td><td data-label=\"Status\">Covered</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"ID\">REQ-11</td><td data-label=\"Source requirement\">Provide a Search Cruises action.</td><td data-label=\"Covered by\">US1, US5</td><td data-label=\"Acceptance evidence\">US1 AC3; US5 AC1–AC3</td><td data-label=\"Status\">Covered</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"ID\">REQ-14</td><td data-label=\"Source requirement\">Represent the supplied default, open and completed visual states.</td><td data-label=\"Covered by\">US1–US5</td><td data-label=\"Acceptance evidence\">Story-level visual references</td><td data-label=\"Status\">Covered with design-authority assumption</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p></p></section>","us2":"<section class=\"story-header\" id=\"us2-summary\"><h2><span id=\"src-0213\" data-source=\"SRC-0213\">Story 2 — Select a cruise destination</span></h2><p class=\"story-callout\"><span id=\"src-0215\" data-source=\"SRC-0215\">As a consumer, I want to select a cruise destination, so that I can search for cruises visiting a location that interests me.</span></p><p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> US1 · shared controls and panel state</p><p><strong>Scope:</strong> Home Page component; illustrative data and existing design-system assumptions.</p></section><section id=\"us2-value\"><h2>Why it matters</h2><p class=\"story-callout\">Consumers can focus their search on places they want to visit.</p></section><section id=\"us2-criteria\"><h2><span id=\"src-0216\" data-source=\"SRC-0216\">Acceptance criteria</span></h2><article class=\"criterion\" id=\"us2-ac1\"><div class=\"criterion-heading criterion-meta\"><span class=\"badge proposal\">US2 · AC1</span><a href=\"#us2-ac1\" aria-label=\"Link to US2 AC1\">#</a></div><h3><span id=\"src-0217\" data-source=\"SRC-0217\">AC1 — Display available destinations</span></h3><p class=\"scenario\"><span id=\"src-0218\" data-source=\"SRC-0218\">Scenario: Open the Destination filter</span></p><p class=\"gherkin given\"><span id=\"src-0219\" data-source=\"SRC-0219\">Given the Find a Cruise component is displayed</span></p><p class=\"gherkin when\"><span id=\"src-0220\" data-source=\"SRC-0220\">When the consumer opens the Destination filter</span></p><p class=\"gherkin then\"><span id=\"src-0221\" data-source=\"SRC-0221\">Then the Destination panel expands below the filter row</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0222\" data-source=\"SRC-0222\">And the selector displays the 16 supported destinations</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0223\" data-source=\"SRC-0223\">And each displayed destination can be selected</span></p></article><article class=\"criterion\" id=\"us2-ac2\"><div class=\"criterion-heading criterion-meta\"><span class=\"badge proposal\">US2 · AC2</span><a href=\"#us2-ac2\" aria-label=\"Link to US2 AC2\">#</a></div><h3><span id=\"src-0224\" data-source=\"SRC-0224\">AC2 — Select a destination</span></h3><p class=\"scenario\"><span id=\"src-0225\" data-source=\"SRC-0225\">Scenario: Select Alaska as the destination</span></p><p class=\"gherkin given\"><span id=\"src-0226\" data-source=\"SRC-0226\">Given the Destination filter is open</span></p><p class=\"gherkin when\"><span id=\"src-0227\" data-source=\"SRC-0227\">When the consumer selects \"Alaska\"</span></p><p class=\"gherkin then\"><span id=\"src-0228\" data-source=\"SRC-0228\">Then \"Alaska\" becomes the selected destination</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0229\" data-source=\"SRC-0229\">And the filter displays \"Alaska\"</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0230\" data-source=\"SRC-0230\">And \"Any Destination\" is no longer displayed</span></p></article><article class=\"criterion\" id=\"us2-ac3\"><div class=\"criterion-heading criterion-meta\"><span class=\"badge proposal\">US2 · AC3</span><a href=\"#us2-ac3\" aria-label=\"Link to US2 AC3\">#</a></div><h3><span id=\"src-0231\" data-source=\"SRC-0231\">AC3 — Change the destination</span></h3><p class=\"scenario\"><span id=\"src-0232\" data-source=\"SRC-0232\">Scenario: Replace a selected destination</span></p><p class=\"gherkin given\"><span id=\"src-0233\" data-source=\"SRC-0233\">Given \"Alaska\" is the selected destination</span></p><p class=\"gherkin when\"><span id=\"src-0234\" data-source=\"SRC-0234\">When the consumer opens the Destination filter</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0235\" data-source=\"SRC-0235\">And selects \"Europe\"</span></p><p class=\"gherkin then\"><span id=\"src-0236\" data-source=\"SRC-0236\">Then \"Europe\" replaces \"Alaska\"</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0237\" data-source=\"SRC-0237\">And only \"Europe\" remains selected</span></p></article><article class=\"criterion\" id=\"us2-ac4\"><div class=\"criterion-heading criterion-meta\"><span class=\"badge proposal\">US2 · AC4</span><a href=\"#us2-ac4\" aria-label=\"Link to US2 AC4\">#</a></div><h3><span id=\"src-0240\" data-source=\"SRC-0240\">AC4 — Open only one filter panel at a time</span></h3><p class=\"scenario\"><span id=\"src-0241\" data-source=\"SRC-0241\">Scenario: Open this filter while another filter is open</span></p><p class=\"gherkin given\"><span id=\"src-0242\" data-source=\"SRC-0242\">Given another filter panel is open</span></p><p class=\"gherkin when\"><span id=\"src-0243\" data-source=\"SRC-0243\">When the consumer opens this filter</span></p><p class=\"gherkin then\"><span id=\"src-0244\" data-source=\"SRC-0244\">Then the previously open panel closes</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0245\" data-source=\"SRC-0245\">And any existing selection in that filter remains unchanged</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0246\" data-source=\"SRC-0246\">And only this filter panel remains open</span></p></article></section><section id=\"us2-references\"><h2>Visual references</h2><figure><a href=\"../assets/reference-images/03-destination-panel.png\" aria-label=\"Expand reference image 3\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"../assets/reference-images/03-destination-panel.png\" alt=\"Image 3: Find a Cruise component – Select a Destination\"></a><figcaption><span id=\"src-0281\" data-source=\"SRC-0281\">Image 3: Find a Cruise component – Select a Destination</span><small>Source: supplied assessment · reference 3. Activate the image for the full-size view; use Back to return.</small></figcaption></figure></section><section id=\"us2-decisions\"><h2>Decisions &amp; open questions</h2><p>Temporary assumptions are not confirmed answers. Blocking decisions must be resolved before production Engineering.</p><h3><span id=\"src-0249\" data-source=\"SRC-0249\">Blocking questions and notes</span></h3><article class=\"question blocking\" id=\"us2-q1\"><span class=\"badge blocking-status\">Blocking</span> <span class=\"badge decision-status open\" aria-label=\"Open — awaiting owner confirmation\">Open</span><h4><span id=\"src-0254\" data-source=\"SRC-0254\">What is the authoritative source of the 16 destinations?</span></h4><dl><div><dt>Decision owner / domain</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0255\" data-source=\"SRC-0255\">Product Owner / Data Owner / Technical Lead</span></dd></div><div><dt>Temporary assumption</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0256\" data-source=\"SRC-0256\">An existing API or managed configuration supplies the destination IDs and display names.</span></dd></div><div><dt>Source reasoning</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0257\" data-source=\"SRC-0257\">Development requires authoritative values and identifiers.</span></dd></div></dl></article><article class=\"question blocking\" id=\"us2-q2\"><span class=\"badge blocking-status\">Blocking</span> <span class=\"badge decision-status open\" aria-label=\"Open — awaiting owner confirmation\">Open</span><h4><span id=\"src-0258\" data-source=\"SRC-0258\">Is Destination single-select or multi-select?</span></h4><dl><div><dt>Decision owner / domain</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0259\" data-source=\"SRC-0259\">Product Owner</span></dd></div><div><dt>Temporary assumption</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0260\" data-source=\"SRC-0260\">Only one destination may be selected.</span></dd></div><div><dt>Source reasoning</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0261\" data-source=\"SRC-0261\">Cardinality affects the control, state model and search contract.</span></dd></div></dl></article><article class=\"question blocking\" id=\"us2-q3\"><span class=\"badge blocking-status\">Blocking</span> <span class=\"badge decision-status open\" aria-label=\"Open — awaiting owner confirmation\">Open</span><h4><span id=\"src-0262\" data-source=\"SRC-0262\">Do the selected port or dates restrict the available destinations?</span></h4><dl><div><dt>Decision owner / domain</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0263\" data-source=\"SRC-0263\">Product Owner / Technical Lead</span></dd></div><div><dt>Temporary assumption</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0264\" data-source=\"SRC-0264\">Destinations do not change dynamically. Compatibility is evaluated when searching.</span></dd></div><div><dt>Source reasoning</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0265\" data-source=\"SRC-0265\">Cascading behavior would require additional data requests and invalidation rules.</span></dd></div></dl></article><h3><span id=\"src-0266\" data-source=\"SRC-0266\">Non-blocking questions and notes</span></h3><article class=\"question \" id=\"us2-q4\"><span class=\"badge nonblocking-status\">Non-blocking</span> <span class=\"badge decision-status open\" aria-label=\"Open — awaiting owner confirmation\">Open</span><h4><span id=\"src-0271\" data-source=\"SRC-0271\">How can the consumer return to Any Destination?</span></h4><dl><div><dt>Decision owner / domain</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0272\" data-source=\"SRC-0272\">Product Owner / UX Designer</span></dd></div><div><dt>Temporary assumption</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0273\" data-source=\"SRC-0273\">The selector provides a clear action or unrestricted option.</span></dd></div><div><dt>Source reasoning</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0274\" data-source=\"SRC-0274\">Consumers should be able to undo a selection without reloading the page.</span></dd></div></dl></article><article class=\"question \" id=\"us2-q5\"><span class=\"badge nonblocking-status\">Non-blocking</span> <span class=\"badge decision-status open\" aria-label=\"Open — awaiting owner confirmation\">Open</span><h4><span id=\"src-0275\" data-source=\"SRC-0275\">Can the panel be dismissed by clicking outside it or pressing Escape?</span></h4><dl><div><dt>Decision owner / domain</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0276\" data-source=\"SRC-0276\">UX Designer</span></dd></div><div><dt>Temporary assumption</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0277\" data-source=\"SRC-0277\">Both actions close the panel without changing its current selection.</span></dd></div><div><dt>Source reasoning</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0278\" data-source=\"SRC-0278\">These are conventional interaction behaviors.</span></dd></div></dl></article><p class=\"muted\">If an answer changes, review the affected acceptance criteria, interaction states and tests before implementation.</p></section><section id=\"us2-states\"><h2>State transitions</h2><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Current state</th><th scope=\"col\">Consumer action</th><th scope=\"col\">Resulting state</th><th scope=\"col\">Expected visible behavior</th><th scope=\"col\">Related AC</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label=\"Current state\">Initial state</td><td data-label=\"Consumer action\">Opens Destination</td><td data-label=\"Resulting state\">Destination panel open</td><td data-label=\"Expected visible behavior\">The 16 destinations are displayed. Other panels remain closed.</td><td data-label=\"Related AC\">US2 AC1</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Current state\">Any filter panel open</td><td data-label=\"Consumer action\">Opens another filter</td><td data-label=\"Resulting state\">New panel open</td><td data-label=\"Expected visible behavior\">The previous panel closes and its existing selection remains unchanged.</td><td data-label=\"Related AC\">US2 AC4, US3 AC5, US4 AC7</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Current state\">Destination panel open</td><td data-label=\"Consumer action\">Selects a destination</td><td data-label=\"Resulting state\">Destination selected</td><td data-label=\"Expected visible behavior\">The panel closes and the selected destination replaces Any Destination.</td><td data-label=\"Related AC\">US2 AC2</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section id=\"us2-traceability\"><h2>Traceability</h2><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">ID</th><th scope=\"col\">Source requirement</th><th scope=\"col\">Covered by</th><th scope=\"col\">Acceptance evidence</th><th scope=\"col\">Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label=\"ID\">REQ-03</td><td data-label=\"Source requirement\">Display 16 destinations.</td><td data-label=\"Covered by\">US2</td><td data-label=\"Acceptance evidence\">US2 AC1</td><td data-label=\"Status\">Covered; data source pending</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"ID\">REQ-04</td><td data-label=\"Source requirement\">Replace the default destination after selection.</td><td data-label=\"Covered by\">US2</td><td data-label=\"Acceptance evidence\">US2 AC2–AC3</td><td data-label=\"Status\">Covered</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"ID\">REQ-14</td><td data-label=\"Source requirement\">Represent the supplied default, open and completed visual states.</td><td data-label=\"Covered by\">US1–US5</td><td data-label=\"Acceptance evidence\">Story-level visual references</td><td data-label=\"Status\">Covered with design-authority assumption</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p></p></section>","us3":"<section class=\"story-header\" id=\"us3-summary\"><h2><span id=\"src-0286\" data-source=\"SRC-0286\">Story 3 — Select a departure port</span></h2><p class=\"story-callout\"><span id=\"src-0288\" data-source=\"SRC-0288\">As a consumer, I want to select a departure port, so that I can search for cruises departing from a convenient location.</span></p><p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> US1 · shared controls and panel state</p><p><strong>Scope:</strong> Home Page component; illustrative data and existing design-system assumptions.</p></section><section id=\"us3-value\"><h2>Why it matters</h2><p class=\"story-callout\">Consumers can choose a departure point that fits their travel plans.</p></section><section id=\"us3-criteria\"><h2><span id=\"src-0289\" data-source=\"SRC-0289\">Acceptance criteria</span></h2><article class=\"criterion\" id=\"us3-ac1\"><div class=\"criterion-heading criterion-meta\"><span class=\"badge proposal\">US3 · AC1</span><a href=\"#us3-ac1\" aria-label=\"Link to US3 AC1\">#</a></div><h3><span id=\"src-0290\" data-source=\"SRC-0290\">AC1 — Display the port regions</span></h3><p class=\"scenario\"><span id=\"src-0291\" data-source=\"SRC-0291\">Scenario: Open the Departure Port filter</span></p><p class=\"gherkin given\"><span id=\"src-0292\" data-source=\"SRC-0292\">Given the Find a Cruise component is displayed</span></p><p class=\"gherkin when\"><span id=\"src-0293\" data-source=\"SRC-0293\">When the consumer opens the Departure Port filter</span></p><p class=\"gherkin then\"><span id=\"src-0294\" data-source=\"SRC-0294\">Then the selector displays the five supported regions</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0295\" data-source=\"SRC-0295\">And one region is presented as active</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0296\" data-source=\"SRC-0296\">And the ports belonging to the active region are displayed</span></p><p><span id=\"src-0297\" data-source=\"SRC-0297\">The supported regions are:</span></p><p class=\"bullet clean-bullet\"><span id=\"src-0298\" data-source=\"SRC-0298\">* North America.</span></p><p class=\"bullet clean-bullet\"><span id=\"src-0299\" data-source=\"SRC-0299\">* Caribbean.</span></p><p class=\"bullet clean-bullet\"><span id=\"src-0300\" data-source=\"SRC-0300\">* Europe.</span></p><p class=\"bullet clean-bullet\"><span id=\"src-0301\" data-source=\"SRC-0301\">* Australia.</span></p><p class=\"bullet clean-bullet\"><span id=\"src-0302\" data-source=\"SRC-0302\">* Asia.</span></p></article><article class=\"criterion\" id=\"us3-ac2\"><div class=\"criterion-heading criterion-meta\"><span class=\"badge proposal\">US3 · AC2</span><a href=\"#us3-ac2\" aria-label=\"Link to US3 AC2\">#</a></div><h3><span id=\"src-0303\" data-source=\"SRC-0303\">AC2 — Browse ports by region</span></h3><p class=\"scenario\"><span id=\"src-0304\" data-source=\"SRC-0304\">Scenario: View ports from another region</span></p><p class=\"gherkin given\"><span id=\"src-0305\" data-source=\"SRC-0305\">Given the Departure Port filter is open</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0306\" data-source=\"SRC-0306\">And \"North America\" is the active region</span></p><p class=\"gherkin when\"><span id=\"src-0307\" data-source=\"SRC-0307\">When the consumer selects \"Europe\"</span></p><p class=\"gherkin then\"><span id=\"src-0308\" data-source=\"SRC-0308\">Then \"Europe\" becomes the active region</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0309\" data-source=\"SRC-0309\">And the ports assigned to Europe are displayed</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0310\" data-source=\"SRC-0310\">And no departure port is selected as a result of changing regions</span></p></article><article class=\"criterion\" id=\"us3-ac3\"><div class=\"criterion-heading criterion-meta\"><span class=\"badge proposal\">US3 · AC3</span><a href=\"#us3-ac3\" aria-label=\"Link to US3 AC3\">#</a></div><h3><span id=\"src-0311\" data-source=\"SRC-0311\">AC3 — Select a departure port</span></h3><p class=\"scenario\"><span id=\"src-0312\" data-source=\"SRC-0312\">Scenario: Select Seattle as the departure port</span></p><p class=\"gherkin given\"><span id=\"src-0313\" data-source=\"SRC-0313\">Given the Departure Port filter is open</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0314\" data-source=\"SRC-0314\">And North America is the active region</span></p><p class=\"gherkin when\"><span id=\"src-0315\" data-source=\"SRC-0315\">When the consumer selects \"Seattle, Washington\"</span></p><p class=\"gherkin then\"><span id=\"src-0316\" data-source=\"SRC-0316\">Then \"Seattle, Washington\" becomes the selected departure port</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0317\" data-source=\"SRC-0317\">And it replaces \"Any Departure Port\"</span></p></article><article class=\"criterion\" id=\"us3-ac4\"><div class=\"criterion-heading criterion-meta\"><span class=\"badge proposal\">US3 · AC4</span><a href=\"#us3-ac4\" aria-label=\"Link to US3 AC4\">#</a></div><h3><span id=\"src-0318\" data-source=\"SRC-0318\">AC4 — Change the departure port</span></h3><p class=\"scenario\"><span id=\"src-0319\" data-source=\"SRC-0319\">Scenario: Replace a selected departure port</span></p><p class=\"gherkin given\"><span id=\"src-0320\" data-source=\"SRC-0320\">Given \"Seattle, Washington\" is selected</span></p><p class=\"gherkin when\"><span id=\"src-0321\" data-source=\"SRC-0321\">When the consumer selects \"Miami, Florida\"</span></p><p class=\"gherkin then\"><span id=\"src-0322\" data-source=\"SRC-0322\">Then \"Miami, Florida\" replaces \"Seattle, Washington\"</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0323\" data-source=\"SRC-0323\">And only \"Miami, Florida\" remains selected</span></p></article><article class=\"criterion\" id=\"us3-ac5\"><div class=\"criterion-heading criterion-meta\"><span class=\"badge proposal\">US3 · AC5</span><a href=\"#us3-ac5\" aria-label=\"Link to US3 AC5\">#</a></div><h3><span id=\"src-0326\" data-source=\"SRC-0326\">AC5 — Open only one filter panel at a time</span></h3><p class=\"scenario\"><span id=\"src-0327\" data-source=\"SRC-0327\">Scenario: Open this filter while another filter is open</span></p><p class=\"gherkin given\"><span id=\"src-0328\" data-source=\"SRC-0328\">Given another filter panel is open</span></p><p class=\"gherkin when\"><span id=\"src-0329\" data-source=\"SRC-0329\">When the consumer opens this filter</span></p><p class=\"gherkin then\"><span id=\"src-0330\" data-source=\"SRC-0330\">Then the previously open panel closes</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0331\" data-source=\"SRC-0331\">And any existing selection in that filter remains unchanged</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0332\" data-source=\"SRC-0332\">And only this filter panel remains open</span></p></article></section><section id=\"us3-references\"><h2>Visual references</h2><figure><a href=\"../assets/reference-images/04-departure-port-panel.png\" aria-label=\"Expand reference image 4\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"../assets/reference-images/04-departure-port-panel.png\" alt=\"Image 4: Find a Cruise component – Select a Departure Port\"></a><figcaption><span id=\"src-0365\" data-source=\"SRC-0365\">Image 4: Find a Cruise component – Select a Departure Port</span><small>Source: supplied assessment · reference 4. Activate the image for the full-size view; use Back to return.</small></figcaption></figure></section><section id=\"us3-decisions\"><h2>Decisions &amp; open questions</h2><p>Temporary assumptions are not confirmed answers. Blocking decisions must be resolved before production Engineering.</p><h3><span id=\"src-0333\" data-source=\"SRC-0333\">Blocking questions and notes</span></h3><article class=\"question blocking\" id=\"us3-q1\"><span class=\"badge blocking-status\">Blocking</span> <span class=\"badge decision-status open\" aria-label=\"Open — awaiting owner confirmation\">Open</span><h4><span id=\"src-0338\" data-source=\"SRC-0338\">What is the authoritative source of departure ports and their region assignments?</span></h4><dl><div><dt>Decision owner / domain</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0339\" data-source=\"SRC-0339\">Product Owner / Data Owner / Technical Lead</span></dd></div><div><dt>Temporary assumption</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0340\" data-source=\"SRC-0340\">An existing API or configuration supplies each port’s canonical ID, display name and region.</span></dd></div><div><dt>Source reasoning</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0341\" data-source=\"SRC-0341\">Development cannot populate or group ports without an authoritative structure.</span></dd></div></dl></article><article class=\"question blocking\" id=\"us3-q2\"><span class=\"badge blocking-status\">Blocking</span> <span class=\"badge decision-status open\" aria-label=\"Open — awaiting owner confirmation\">Open</span><h4><span id=\"src-0342\" data-source=\"SRC-0342\">Is Departure Port single-select or multi-select?</span></h4><dl><div><dt>Decision owner / domain</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0343\" data-source=\"SRC-0343\">Product Owner</span></dd></div><div><dt>Temporary assumption</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0344\" data-source=\"SRC-0344\">Only one departure port may be selected.</span></dd></div><div><dt>Source reasoning</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0345\" data-source=\"SRC-0345\">Cardinality affects the control and search contract.</span></dd></div></dl></article><article class=\"question blocking\" id=\"us3-q3\"><span class=\"badge blocking-status\">Blocking</span> <span class=\"badge decision-status open\" aria-label=\"Open — awaiting owner confirmation\">Open</span><h4><span id=\"src-0346\" data-source=\"SRC-0346\">Does the selected destination restrict the available departure ports?</span></h4><dl><div><dt>Decision owner / domain</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0347\" data-source=\"SRC-0347\">Product Owner / Technical Lead</span></dd></div><div><dt>Temporary assumption</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0348\" data-source=\"SRC-0348\">Selecting a destination does not dynamically restrict ports. Incompatible combinations may produce no results.</span></dd></div><div><dt>Source reasoning</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0349\" data-source=\"SRC-0349\">Dynamic dependency would materially change state and data-loading behavior.</span></dd></div></dl></article><h3><span id=\"src-0350\" data-source=\"SRC-0350\">Non-blocking questions and notes</span></h3><article class=\"question \" id=\"us3-q4\"><span class=\"badge nonblocking-status\">Non-blocking</span> <span class=\"badge decision-status open\" aria-label=\"Open — awaiting owner confirmation\">Open</span><h4><span id=\"src-0355\" data-source=\"SRC-0355\">Which region is initially active?</span></h4><dl><div><dt>Decision owner / domain</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0356\" data-source=\"SRC-0356\">Product Owner / UX Designer</span></dd></div><div><dt>Temporary assumption</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0357\" data-source=\"SRC-0357\">North America is active by default, as shown in Visual Reference 4.</span></dd></div><div><dt>Source reasoning</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0358\" data-source=\"SRC-0358\">This follows the supplied reference without introducing a new rule.</span></dd></div></dl></article><article class=\"question \" id=\"us3-q5\"><span class=\"badge nonblocking-status\">Non-blocking</span> <span class=\"badge decision-status open\" aria-label=\"Open — awaiting owner confirmation\">Open</span><h4><span id=\"src-0359\" data-source=\"SRC-0359\">How can the consumer return to Any Departure Port?</span></h4><dl><div><dt>Decision owner / domain</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0360\" data-source=\"SRC-0360\">Product Owner / UX Designer</span></dd></div><div><dt>Temporary assumption</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0361\" data-source=\"SRC-0361\">The selector provides a clear action or unrestricted option.</span></dd></div><div><dt>Source reasoning</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0362\" data-source=\"SRC-0362\">Consumers should be able to remove the restriction.</span></dd></div></dl></article><p class=\"muted\">If an answer changes, review the affected acceptance criteria, interaction states and tests before implementation.</p></section><section id=\"us3-states\"><h2>State transitions</h2><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Current state</th><th scope=\"col\">Consumer action</th><th scope=\"col\">Resulting state</th><th scope=\"col\">Expected visible behavior</th><th scope=\"col\">Related AC</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label=\"Current state\">Any filter panel open</td><td data-label=\"Consumer action\">Opens another filter</td><td data-label=\"Resulting state\">New panel open</td><td data-label=\"Expected visible behavior\">The previous panel closes and its existing selection remains unchanged.</td><td data-label=\"Related AC\">US2 AC4, US3 AC5, US4 AC7</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Current state\">Port panel open</td><td data-label=\"Consumer action\">Selects another region</td><td data-label=\"Resulting state\">Port panel remains open</td><td data-label=\"Expected visible behavior\">Ports for the selected region are displayed. No port is selected as a result of changing regions.</td><td data-label=\"Related AC\">US3 AC2</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Current state\">Port panel open</td><td data-label=\"Consumer action\">Selects a port</td><td data-label=\"Resulting state\">Port selected</td><td data-label=\"Expected visible behavior\">The selected port replaces Any Departure Port.</td><td data-label=\"Related AC\">US3 AC3</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section id=\"us3-traceability\"><h2>Traceability</h2><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">ID</th><th scope=\"col\">Source requirement</th><th scope=\"col\">Covered by</th><th scope=\"col\">Acceptance evidence</th><th scope=\"col\">Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label=\"ID\">REQ-05</td><td data-label=\"Source requirement\">Display ports from five regions.</td><td data-label=\"Covered by\">US3</td><td data-label=\"Acceptance evidence\">US3 AC1–AC2</td><td data-label=\"Status\">Covered; data source pending</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"ID\">REQ-06</td><td data-label=\"Source requirement\">Replace the default port after selection.</td><td data-label=\"Covered by\">US3</td><td data-label=\"Acceptance evidence\">US3 AC3–AC4</td><td data-label=\"Status\">Covered</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"ID\">REQ-14</td><td data-label=\"Source requirement\">Represent the supplied default, open and completed visual states.</td><td data-label=\"Covered by\">US1–US5</td><td data-label=\"Acceptance evidence\">Story-level visual references</td><td data-label=\"Status\">Covered with design-authority assumption</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p></p></section>","us4":"<section class=\"story-header\" id=\"us4-summary\"><h2><span id=\"src-0370\" data-source=\"SRC-0370\">Story 4 — Select a departure month range</span></h2><p class=\"story-callout\"><span id=\"src-0372\" data-source=\"SRC-0372\">As a consumer, I want to select a departure month range, so that I can search for cruises sailing during a period that works for me.</span></p><p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> US1 · calendar availability and date decisions</p><p><strong>Scope:</strong> Home Page component; illustrative data and existing design-system assumptions.</p></section><section id=\"us4-value\"><h2>Why it matters</h2><p class=\"story-callout\">Consumers can find sailings within the period when they are able to travel.</p></section><section id=\"us4-criteria\"><h2><span id=\"src-0373\" data-source=\"SRC-0373\">Acceptance criteria</span></h2><article class=\"criterion\" id=\"us4-ac1\"><div class=\"criterion-heading criterion-meta\"><span class=\"badge proposal\">US4 · AC1</span><a href=\"#us4-ac1\" aria-label=\"Link to US4 AC1\">#</a></div><h3><span id=\"src-0374\" data-source=\"SRC-0374\">AC1 — Display the four-year period</span></h3><p class=\"scenario\"><span id=\"src-0375\" data-source=\"SRC-0375\">Scenario: Display the departure month selector</span></p><p class=\"gherkin given\"><span id=\"src-0376\" data-source=\"SRC-0376\">Given the current calendar year is 2026</span></p><p class=\"gherkin when\"><span id=\"src-0377\" data-source=\"SRC-0377\">When the consumer opens the Departure Date filter</span></p><p class=\"gherkin then\"><span id=\"src-0378\" data-source=\"SRC-0378\">Then the selector displays 2026, 2027, 2028 and 2029</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0379\" data-source=\"SRC-0379\">And each year displays its twelve calendar months</span></p></article><article class=\"criterion\" id=\"us4-ac2\"><div class=\"criterion-heading criterion-meta\"><span class=\"badge proposal\">US4 · AC2</span><a href=\"#us4-ac2\" aria-label=\"Link to US4 AC2\">#</a></div><h3><span id=\"src-0380\" data-source=\"SRC-0380\">AC2 — Differentiate available and unavailable months</span></h3><p class=\"scenario\"><span id=\"src-0381\" data-source=\"SRC-0381\">Scenario: Prevent selection of a month without available sailings</span></p><p class=\"gherkin given\"><span id=\"src-0382\" data-source=\"SRC-0382\">Given the search capability indicates that June 2028 has no available sailings</span></p><p class=\"gherkin when\"><span id=\"src-0383\" data-source=\"SRC-0383\">When the Departure Date filter is displayed</span></p><p class=\"gherkin then\"><span id=\"src-0384\" data-source=\"SRC-0384\">Then June 2028 is presented as unavailable</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0385\" data-source=\"SRC-0385\">And the consumer cannot select June 2028</span></p><p><span id=\"src-0386\" data-source=\"SRC-0386\">Temporary assumption: month availability is global and does not change according to the destination or departure port selections.</span></p></article><article class=\"criterion\" id=\"us4-ac3\"><div class=\"criterion-heading criterion-meta\"><span class=\"badge proposal\">US4 · AC3</span><a href=\"#us4-ac3\" aria-label=\"Link to US4 AC3\">#</a></div><h3><span id=\"src-0389\" data-source=\"SRC-0389\">AC3 — Select the start month</span></h3><p class=\"scenario\"><span id=\"src-0390\" data-source=\"SRC-0390\">Scenario: Select the first month of the range</span></p><p class=\"gherkin given\"><span id=\"src-0391\" data-source=\"SRC-0391\">Given May 2027 has available sailings</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0392\" data-source=\"SRC-0392\">And no departure month has been selected</span></p><p class=\"gherkin when\"><span id=\"src-0393\" data-source=\"SRC-0393\">When the consumer selects May 2027</span></p><p class=\"gherkin then\"><span id=\"src-0394\" data-source=\"SRC-0394\">Then May 2027 becomes the start month</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0395\" data-source=\"SRC-0395\">And the selector remains open for the end-month selection</span></p></article><article class=\"criterion\" id=\"us4-ac4\"><div class=\"criterion-heading criterion-meta\"><span class=\"badge proposal\">US4 · AC4</span><a href=\"#us4-ac4\" aria-label=\"Link to US4 AC4\">#</a></div><h3><span id=\"src-0396\" data-source=\"SRC-0396\">AC4 — Complete the range</span></h3><p class=\"scenario\"><span id=\"src-0397\" data-source=\"SRC-0397\">Scenario: Select a valid departure month range</span></p><p class=\"gherkin given\"><span id=\"src-0398\" data-source=\"SRC-0398\">Given May 2027 is the selected start month</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0399\" data-source=\"SRC-0399\">And September 2027 has available sailings</span></p><p class=\"gherkin when\"><span id=\"src-0400\" data-source=\"SRC-0400\">When the consumer selects September 2027</span></p><p class=\"gherkin then\"><span id=\"src-0401\" data-source=\"SRC-0401\">Then September 2027 becomes the end month</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0402\" data-source=\"SRC-0402\">And the inclusive range is May 2027 through September 2027</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0403\" data-source=\"SRC-0403\">And the filter displays \"May '27 - Sep '27\"</span></p></article><article class=\"criterion\" id=\"us4-ac5\"><div class=\"criterion-heading criterion-meta\"><span class=\"badge proposal\">US4 · AC5</span><a href=\"#us4-ac5\" aria-label=\"Link to US4 AC5\">#</a></div><h3><span id=\"src-0404\" data-source=\"SRC-0404\">AC5 — Select a range across calendar years</span></h3><p class=\"scenario\"><span id=\"src-0405\" data-source=\"SRC-0405\">Scenario: Select a range spanning two calendar years</span></p><p class=\"gherkin given\"><span id=\"src-0406\" data-source=\"SRC-0406\">Given November 2027 is the selected start month</span></p><p class=\"gherkin when\"><span id=\"src-0407\" data-source=\"SRC-0407\">When the consumer selects February 2028</span></p><p class=\"gherkin then\"><span id=\"src-0408\" data-source=\"SRC-0408\">Then the range is November 2027 through February 2028</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0409\" data-source=\"SRC-0409\">And the filter displays both boundary months</span></p></article><article class=\"criterion\" id=\"us4-ac6\"><div class=\"criterion-heading criterion-meta\"><span class=\"badge proposal\">US4 · AC6</span><a href=\"#us4-ac6\" aria-label=\"Link to US4 AC6\">#</a></div><h3><span id=\"src-0410\" data-source=\"SRC-0410\">AC6 — Select an earlier second month</span></h3><p><span id=\"src-0411\" data-source=\"SRC-0411\">This behavior requires Product Owner confirmation.</span></p><p class=\"scenario\"><span id=\"src-0412\" data-source=\"SRC-0412\">Scenario: Select a month earlier than the current start month</span></p><p class=\"gherkin given\"><span id=\"src-0413\" data-source=\"SRC-0413\">Given September 2027 is the selected start month</span></p><p class=\"gherkin when\"><span id=\"src-0414\" data-source=\"SRC-0414\">When the consumer selects May 2027</span></p><p class=\"gherkin then\"><span id=\"src-0415\" data-source=\"SRC-0415\">Then May 2027 becomes the new start month</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0416\" data-source=\"SRC-0416\">And no end month is selected</span></p></article><article class=\"criterion\" id=\"us4-ac7\"><div class=\"criterion-heading criterion-meta\"><span class=\"badge proposal\">US4 · AC7</span><a href=\"#us4-ac7\" aria-label=\"Link to US4 AC7\">#</a></div><h3><span id=\"src-0419\" data-source=\"SRC-0419\">AC7 — Open only one filter panel at a time</span></h3><p class=\"scenario\"><span id=\"src-0420\" data-source=\"SRC-0420\">Scenario: Open this filter while another filter is open</span></p><p class=\"gherkin given\"><span id=\"src-0421\" data-source=\"SRC-0421\">Given another filter panel is open</span></p><p class=\"gherkin when\"><span id=\"src-0422\" data-source=\"SRC-0422\">When the consumer opens this filter</span></p><p class=\"gherkin then\"><span id=\"src-0423\" data-source=\"SRC-0423\">Then the previously open panel closes</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0424\" data-source=\"SRC-0424\">And any existing selection in that filter remains unchanged</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0425\" data-source=\"SRC-0425\">And only this filter panel remains open</span></p></article><article class=\"criterion\" id=\"us4-ac8\"><h3>AC8 — Past months remain visible but disabled</h3><p class=\"gherkin\">Given the calendar is open and the current demonstration month is September 2026</p><p class=\"gherkin\">When the consumer views months before September 2026</p><p class=\"gherkin\">Then January through August 2026 remain visible and disabled</p><p class=\"gherkin\">And they cannot become a range start or end or alter an existing selection</p><p class=\"gherkin\">And September 2026 and future months are selectable only when sailings are available</p></article></section><section id=\"us4-references\"><h2>Visual references</h2><figure><a href=\"../assets/reference-images/05-departure-date-panel.png\" aria-label=\"Expand reference image 5\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"../assets/reference-images/05-departure-date-panel.png\" alt=\"Image 5: Find a Cruise component – Select a Departure Date\"></a><figcaption><span id=\"src-0466\" data-source=\"SRC-0466\">Image 5: Find a Cruise component – Select a Departure Date</span><small>Source: supplied assessment · reference 5. Activate the image for the full-size view; use Back to return.</small></figcaption></figure><figure><a href=\"../assets/reference-images/06-all-selections-populated.png\" aria-label=\"Expand reference image 6\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"../assets/reference-images/06-all-selections-populated.png\" alt=\"Image 6: Find a Cruise component – All selections populated\"></a><figcaption><span id=\"src-0473\" data-source=\"SRC-0473\">Image 6: Find a Cruise component – All selections populated</span><small>Source: supplied assessment · reference 6. Activate the image for the full-size view; use Back to return.</small></figcaption></figure></section><section id=\"us4-decisions\"><h2>Decisions &amp; open questions</h2><p>Temporary assumptions are not confirmed answers. Blocking decisions must be resolved before production Engineering.</p><h3><span id=\"src-0426\" data-source=\"SRC-0426\">Blocking questions and notes</span></h3><article class=\"question blocking\" id=\"us4-q1\"><span class=\"badge blocking-status\">Blocking</span> <span class=\"badge decision-status open\" aria-label=\"Open — awaiting owner confirmation\">Open</span><h4><span id=\"src-0431\" data-source=\"SRC-0431\">Does “four-year calendar” mean four calendar years or a rolling 48-month period?</span></h4><dl><div><dt>Decision owner / domain</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0432\" data-source=\"SRC-0432\">Product Owner</span></dd></div><div><dt>Temporary assumption</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0433\" data-source=\"SRC-0433\">It means the current calendar year plus the following three calendar years.</span></dd></div><div><dt>Source reasoning</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0434\" data-source=\"SRC-0434\">This determines which months are displayed and requested.</span></dd></div></dl></article><article class=\"question blocking\" id=\"us4-q2\"><span class=\"badge blocking-status\">Blocking</span> <span class=\"badge decision-status open\" aria-label=\"Open — awaiting owner confirmation\">Open</span><h4><span id=\"src-0435\" data-source=\"SRC-0435\">Can the same month be selected as both start and end?</span></h4><dl><div><dt>Decision owner / domain</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0436\" data-source=\"SRC-0436\">Product Owner</span></dd></div><div><dt>Temporary assumption</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0437\" data-source=\"SRC-0437\">Yes. Selecting the same month twice creates a one-month range.</span></dd></div><div><dt>Source reasoning</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0438\" data-source=\"SRC-0438\">Consumers may want to search within one month.</span></dd></div></dl></article><article class=\"question blocking\" id=\"us4-q3\"><span class=\"badge blocking-status\">Blocking</span> <span class=\"badge decision-status open\" aria-label=\"Open — awaiting owner confirmation\">Open</span><h4><span id=\"src-0439\" data-source=\"SRC-0439\">What happens when the second selected month is earlier than the first?</span></h4><dl><div><dt>Decision owner / domain</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0440\" data-source=\"SRC-0440\">Product Owner / UX Designer</span></dd></div><div><dt>Temporary assumption</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0441\" data-source=\"SRC-0441\">The second selection becomes the new start and the previous partial selection is cleared.</span></dd></div><div><dt>Source reasoning</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0442\" data-source=\"SRC-0442\">This defines a central transition in the selector state model.</span></dd></div></dl></article><article class=\"question blocking\" id=\"us4-q4\"><span class=\"badge blocking-status\">Blocking</span> <span class=\"badge decision-status open\" aria-label=\"Open — awaiting owner confirmation\">Open</span><h4><span id=\"src-0443\" data-source=\"SRC-0443\">What happens if the consumer exits after selecting only a start month?</span></h4><dl><div><dt>Decision owner / domain</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0444\" data-source=\"SRC-0444\">Product Owner / UX Designer</span></dd></div><div><dt>Temporary assumption</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0445\" data-source=\"SRC-0445\">An incomplete range is not applied and the filter continues to represent Any Date.</span></dd></div><div><dt>Source reasoning</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0446\" data-source=\"SRC-0446\">Development must know whether a single selection is a valid criterion.</span></dd></div></dl></article><article class=\"question blocking\" id=\"us4-q5\"><span class=\"badge blocking-status\">Blocking</span> <span class=\"badge decision-status open\" aria-label=\"Open — awaiting owner confirmation\">Open</span><h4><span id=\"src-0447\" data-source=\"SRC-0447\">Does month availability depend on the selected destination and departure port?</span></h4><dl><div><dt>Decision owner / domain</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0448\" data-source=\"SRC-0448\">Product Owner / Technical Lead</span></dd></div><div><dt>Temporary assumption</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0449\" data-source=\"SRC-0449\">Month availability is global. A month is selectable when at least one sailing is available during that month, independently of the other filter selections.</span></dd></div><div><dt>Source reasoning</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0450\" data-source=\"SRC-0450\">Contextual availability would introduce dependencies between filters, recalculation rules and handling for selections that become invalid. None of this behavior is defined in the requirement.</span></dd></div></dl></article><h3><span id=\"src-0451\" data-source=\"SRC-0451\">Non-blocking questions and notes</span></h3><article class=\"question \" id=\"us4-q6\"><span class=\"badge nonblocking-status\">Non-blocking</span> <span class=\"badge decision-status confirmed\" aria-label=\"Confirmed for this proposal\">Confirmed</span><h4><span id=\"src-0456\" data-source=\"SRC-0456\">Are past months hidden or disabled?</span></h4><dl><div><dt>Decision owner / domain</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0457\" data-source=\"SRC-0457\">Product Owner / UX Designer</span></dd></div><div><dt>Agreed behavior</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0458\" data-source=\"SRC-0458\">Past months remain visible but disabled.</span></dd></div><div><dt>Source reasoning</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0459\" data-source=\"SRC-0459\">The supplied reference already defines a disabled state.</span></dd></div></dl></article><article class=\"question \" id=\"us4-q7\"><span class=\"badge nonblocking-status\">Non-blocking</span> <span class=\"badge decision-status open\" aria-label=\"Open — awaiting owner confirmation\">Open</span><h4><span id=\"src-0460\" data-source=\"SRC-0460\">What happens when a third month is selected after completing a range?</span></h4><dl><div><dt>Decision owner / domain</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0461\" data-source=\"SRC-0461\">Product Owner / UX Designer</span></dd></div><div><dt>Temporary assumption</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0462\" data-source=\"SRC-0462\">The third selection starts a new range.</span></dd></div><div><dt>Source reasoning</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0463\" data-source=\"SRC-0463\">This provides a predictable replacement interaction.</span></dd></div></dl></article><p class=\"muted\">If an answer changes, review the affected acceptance criteria, interaction states and tests before implementation.</p></section><section id=\"us4-states\"><h2>State transitions</h2><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Current state</th><th scope=\"col\">Consumer action</th><th scope=\"col\">Resulting state</th><th scope=\"col\">Expected visible behavior</th><th scope=\"col\">Related AC</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label=\"Current state\">Any filter panel open</td><td data-label=\"Consumer action\">Opens another filter</td><td data-label=\"Resulting state\">New panel open</td><td data-label=\"Expected visible behavior\">The previous panel closes and its existing selection remains unchanged.</td><td data-label=\"Related AC\">US2 AC4, US3 AC5, US4 AC7</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Current state\">Date panel open</td><td data-label=\"Consumer action\">Selects an unavailable month</td><td data-label=\"Resulting state\">No state change</td><td data-label=\"Expected visible behavior\">The month cannot be selected.</td><td data-label=\"Related AC\">US4 AC2</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Current state\">Date panel open</td><td data-label=\"Consumer action\">Selects the first available month</td><td data-label=\"Resulting state\">Partial date-range state</td><td data-label=\"Expected visible behavior\">The month becomes the start month. The panel remains open and Any Date continues to represent the applied criterion.</td><td data-label=\"Related AC\">US4 AC3, US4 blocking question</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Current state\">Partial date range</td><td data-label=\"Consumer action\">Selects a valid end month</td><td data-label=\"Resulting state\">Completed date-range state</td><td data-label=\"Expected visible behavior\">The completed range replaces Any Date.</td><td data-label=\"Related AC\">US4 AC4</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Current state\">Partial date range</td><td data-label=\"Consumer action\">Selects an earlier month</td><td data-label=\"Resulting state\">New partial date-range state</td><td data-label=\"Expected visible behavior\">The new month becomes the start and no end month remains selected.</td><td data-label=\"Related AC\">US4 AC6</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Current state\">Completed date range</td><td data-label=\"Consumer action\">Starts another selection</td><td data-label=\"Resulting state\">New partial date-range state</td><td data-label=\"Expected visible behavior\">The previous range is replaced by the new start month.</td><td data-label=\"Related AC\">US4 non-blocking question</td></tr><tr><td>Date panel open</td><td>Attempt to choose a past month</td><td>Selection unchanged</td><td>Past months stay visible and disabled; current month follows availability.</td><td>US4 AC8</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section id=\"us4-traceability\"><h2>Traceability</h2><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">ID</th><th scope=\"col\">Source requirement</th><th scope=\"col\">Covered by</th><th scope=\"col\">Acceptance evidence</th><th scope=\"col\">Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label=\"ID\">REQ-07</td><td data-label=\"Source requirement\">Display a four-year calendar.</td><td data-label=\"Covered by\">US4</td><td data-label=\"Acceptance evidence\">US4 AC1</td><td data-label=\"Status\">Covered with assumption</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"ID\">REQ-08</td><td data-label=\"Source requirement\">Only current or future months with available sailings are selectable.</td><td data-label=\"Covered by\">US4</td><td data-label=\"Acceptance evidence\">US4 AC2, AC8</td><td data-label=\"Status\">Past-month behavior agreed; availability dependency on other filters pending confirmation.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"ID\">REQ-09</td><td data-label=\"Source requirement\">Use the first month as start and the second as end.</td><td data-label=\"Covered by\">US4</td><td data-label=\"Acceptance evidence\">US4 AC3–AC6</td><td data-label=\"Status\">Covered with assumptions</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"ID\">REQ-10</td><td data-label=\"Source requirement\">Replace Any Date with the completed range.</td><td data-label=\"Covered by\">US4</td><td data-label=\"Acceptance evidence\">US4 AC4–AC5</td><td data-label=\"Status\">Covered</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"ID\">REQ-14</td><td data-label=\"Source requirement\">Represent the supplied default, open and completed visual states.</td><td data-label=\"Covered by\">US1–US5</td><td data-label=\"Acceptance evidence\">Story-level visual references</td><td data-label=\"Status\">Covered with design-authority assumption</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p></p></section>","us5":"<section class=\"story-header\" id=\"us5-summary\"><h2><span id=\"src-0476\" data-source=\"SRC-0476\">Story 5 — Search for cruises using selected filters</span></h2><p class=\"story-callout\"><span id=\"src-0478\" data-source=\"SRC-0478\">As a consumer, I want to search for cruises using my selected preferences, so that I can review sailings relevant to my destination, departure port and travel period.</span></p><h3><span id=\"src-0479\" data-source=\"SRC-0479\">Scope assumption</span></h3><p><span id=\"src-0480\" data-source=\"SRC-0480\">The existing search capability can receive the consumer’s selected search criteria and apply them on the Cruises page. The mechanism used to transfer those criteria is outside the scope of this exercise.</span></p><p><strong>Dependencies:</strong> US1–US4 · completed criteria and external results capability</p><p><strong>Scope:</strong> Product handoff to /cruises; prototype simulates applicable criteria only.</p></section><section id=\"us5-value\"><h2>Why it matters</h2><p class=\"story-callout\">Consumers can continue exploring cruise options without re-entering their preferences.</p></section><section id=\"us5-criteria\"><h2><span id=\"src-0481\" data-source=\"SRC-0481\">Acceptance criteria</span></h2><article class=\"criterion\" id=\"us5-ac1\"><div class=\"criterion-heading criterion-meta\"><span class=\"badge proposal\">US5 · AC1</span><a href=\"#us5-ac1\" aria-label=\"Link to US5 AC1\">#</a></div><h3><span id=\"src-0482\" data-source=\"SRC-0482\">AC1 — Search with all filters</span></h3><p class=\"scenario\"><span id=\"src-0483\" data-source=\"SRC-0483\">Scenario: Search using destination, port and departure range</span></p><p class=\"gherkin given\"><span id=\"src-0484\" data-source=\"SRC-0484\">Given the consumer selected \"Alaska\"</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0485\" data-source=\"SRC-0485\">And selected \"Seattle, Washington\"</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0486\" data-source=\"SRC-0486\">And selected May 2027 through September 2027</span></p><p class=\"gherkin when\"><span id=\"src-0487\" data-source=\"SRC-0487\">When the consumer selects \"Search Cruises\"</span></p><p class=\"gherkin then\"><span id=\"src-0488\" data-source=\"SRC-0488\">Then the consumer is redirected to \"/cruises\"</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0489\" data-source=\"SRC-0489\">And the destination filter is set to \"Alaska\"</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0490\" data-source=\"SRC-0490\">And the departure port filter is set to \"Seattle, Washington\"</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0491\" data-source=\"SRC-0491\">And the departure date filter is set to May 2027 through September 2027</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0492\" data-source=\"SRC-0492\">And the displayed results conform to all three filters</span></p></article><article class=\"criterion\" id=\"us5-ac2\"><div class=\"criterion-heading criterion-meta\"><span class=\"badge proposal\">US5 · AC2</span><a href=\"#us5-ac2\" aria-label=\"Link to US5 AC2\">#</a></div><h3><span id=\"src-0493\" data-source=\"SRC-0493\">AC2 — Search with at least one selected filter</span></h3><p class=\"scenario\"><span id=\"src-0494\" data-source=\"SRC-0494\">Scenario: Search using only a destination</span></p><p class=\"gherkin given\"><span id=\"src-0495\" data-source=\"SRC-0495\">Given the consumer selected “Alaska” as the destination</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0496\" data-source=\"SRC-0496\">And the Departure Port filter displays “Any Departure Port”</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0497\" data-source=\"SRC-0497\">And the Departure Date filter displays “Any Date”</span></p><p class=\"gherkin when\"><span id=\"src-0498\" data-source=\"SRC-0498\">When the consumer selects “Search Cruises”</span></p><p class=\"gherkin then\"><span id=\"src-0499\" data-source=\"SRC-0499\">Then the consumer is redirected to /cruises</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0500\" data-source=\"SRC-0500\">And the displayed results are restricted to the selected destination</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0501\" data-source=\"SRC-0501\">And the unselected filters do not restrict the results</span></p></article><article class=\"criterion\" id=\"us5-ac3\"><div class=\"criterion-heading criterion-meta\"><span class=\"badge proposal\">US5 · AC3</span><a href=\"#us5-ac3\" aria-label=\"Link to US5 AC3\">#</a></div><h3><span id=\"src-0502\" data-source=\"SRC-0502\">AC3 — Prevent a search without any selected criteria</span></h3><p class=\"scenario\"><span id=\"src-0503\" data-source=\"SRC-0503\">Scenario: Attempt to search without selecting any filter</span></p><p class=\"gherkin given\"><span id=\"src-0504\" data-source=\"SRC-0504\">Given all three filters display their default “Any” values</span></p><p class=\"gherkin when\"><span id=\"src-0505\" data-source=\"SRC-0505\">When the consumer attempts to start the search</span></p><p class=\"gherkin then\"><span id=\"src-0506\" data-source=\"SRC-0506\">Then the search is not initiated</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0507\" data-source=\"SRC-0507\">And the consumer is informed that at least one search criterion must be selected</span></p><p><span id=\"src-0508\" data-source=\"SRC-0508\">Temporary behavior pending Product Owner confirmation of the minimum required selection</span></p></article><article class=\"criterion\" id=\"us5-ac4\"><div class=\"criterion-heading criterion-meta\"><span class=\"badge proposal\">US5 · AC4</span><a href=\"#us5-ac4\" aria-label=\"Link to US5 AC4\">#</a></div><h3><span id=\"src-0511\" data-source=\"SRC-0511\">AC4 — Display the applied search criteria</span></h3><p class=\"scenario\"><span id=\"src-0512\" data-source=\"SRC-0512\">Scenario: Preserve search state on the results page</span></p><p class=\"gherkin given\"><span id=\"src-0513\" data-source=\"SRC-0513\">Given the consumer initiated a search from the Home Page</span></p><p class=\"gherkin when\"><span id=\"src-0514\" data-source=\"SRC-0514\">When the results page loads successfully</span></p><p class=\"gherkin then\"><span id=\"src-0515\" data-source=\"SRC-0515\">Then each criterion selected on the Home Page is displayed as selected</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0516\" data-source=\"SRC-0516\">And the visible filter state corresponds to the criteria used to retrieve the results</span></p></article><article class=\"criterion\" id=\"us5-ac5\"><div class=\"criterion-heading criterion-meta\"><span class=\"badge proposal\">US5 · AC5</span><a href=\"#us5-ac5\" aria-label=\"Link to US5 AC5\">#</a></div><h3><span id=\"src-0517\" data-source=\"SRC-0517\">AC5 — Do not apply an unselected filter</span></h3><p class=\"scenario\"><span id=\"src-0518\" data-source=\"SRC-0518\">Scenario: Search with an unselected destination</span></p><p class=\"gherkin given\"><span id=\"src-0519\" data-source=\"SRC-0519\">Given the Destination filter displays “Any Destination”</span></p><p class=\"gherkin and\"><span id=\"src-0520\" data-source=\"SRC-0520\">And the consumer has completed all required selections</span></p><p class=\"gherkin when\"><span id=\"src-0521\" data-source=\"SRC-0521\">When the consumer selects “Search Cruises”</span></p><p class=\"gherkin then\"><span id=\"src-0522\" data-source=\"SRC-0522\">Then the destination does not restrict the search results</span></p></article></section><section id=\"us5-references\"><h2>Visual references</h2><figure><a href=\"../assets/reference-images/07-search-results-preselected.png\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"../assets/reference-images/07-search-results-preselected.png\" alt=\"Reference 7: Search page with filters preselected\"></a><figcaption>Reference 7 · Supplied assessment. Activate to expand; use Back to return.</figcaption></figure><p>Reference 7 belongs to the results-page boundary. Its reproduction does not imply implemented navigation or search results.</p></section><section id=\"us5-decisions\"><h2>Decisions &amp; open questions</h2><p>Temporary assumptions are not confirmed answers. Blocking decisions must be resolved before production Engineering.</p><h3><span id=\"src-0525\" data-source=\"SRC-0525\">Blocking questions and notes</span></h3><article class=\"question blocking\" id=\"us5-q1\"><span class=\"badge blocking-status\">Blocking</span> <span class=\"badge decision-status open\" aria-label=\"Open — awaiting owner confirmation\">Open</span><h4><span id=\"src-0530\" data-source=\"SRC-0530\">Can the existing Cruises page display and apply every search criterion selected in the Home Page component?</span></h4><dl><div><dt>Decision owner / domain</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0531\" data-source=\"SRC-0531\">Product Owner / Technical Lead</span></dd></div><div><dt>Temporary assumption</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0532\" data-source=\"SRC-0532\">The existing Cruises page displays the selected criteria and applies them to the result set. The integration mechanism is outside the scope of this exercise.</span></dd></div><div><dt>Source reasoning</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0533\" data-source=\"SRC-0533\">If this capability does not exist, additional results-page work enters the scope.</span></dd></div></dl></article><article class=\"question blocking\" id=\"us5-q2\"><span class=\"badge blocking-status\">Blocking</span> <span class=\"badge decision-status open\" aria-label=\"Open — awaiting owner confirmation\">Open</span><h4><span id=\"src-0534\" data-source=\"SRC-0534\">What happens when valid criteria produce no matching cruises?</span></h4><dl><div><dt>Decision owner / domain</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0535\" data-source=\"SRC-0535\">Product Owner / UX Designer</span></dd></div><div><dt>Temporary assumption</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0536\" data-source=\"SRC-0536\">The results page displays a zero-results state, preserves the filters and allows them to be changed.</span></dd></div><div><dt>Source reasoning</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0537\" data-source=\"SRC-0537\">The system should not silently broaden the search.</span></dd></div></dl></article><article class=\"question blocking\" id=\"us5-q3\"><span class=\"badge blocking-status\">Blocking</span> <span class=\"badge decision-status open\" aria-label=\"Open — awaiting owner confirmation\">Open</span><h4><span id=\"src-0538\" data-source=\"SRC-0538\">Which filters, if any, must be selected before the consumer can start a search?</span></h4><dl><div><dt>Decision owner / domain</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0539\" data-source=\"SRC-0539\">Product Owner</span></dd></div><div><dt>Temporary assumption</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0540\" data-source=\"SRC-0540\">At least one filter must be selected. The three filters are individually optional, but an entirely unrestricted search cannot be submitted.</span></dd></div><div><dt>Source reasoning</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0541\" data-source=\"SRC-0541\">The requirement does not define whether the initial state is searchable. This decision determines button enablement, validation behavior and the valid search scenarios.</span></dd></div></dl></article><h3><span id=\"src-0542\" data-source=\"SRC-0542\">Non-blocking questions and notes</span></h3><article class=\"question \" id=\"us5-q4\"><span class=\"badge nonblocking-status\">Non-blocking</span> <span class=\"badge decision-status open\" aria-label=\"Open — awaiting owner confirmation\">Open</span><h4><span id=\"src-0547\" data-source=\"SRC-0547\">What loading behavior follows Search Cruises activation?</span></h4><dl><div><dt>Decision owner / domain</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0548\" data-source=\"SRC-0548\">UX Designer / Technical Lead</span></dd></div><div><dt>Temporary assumption</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0549\" data-source=\"SRC-0549\">The action displays progress and prevents duplicate submission during navigation.</span></dd></div><div><dt>Source reasoning</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0550\" data-source=\"SRC-0550\">Consumers need feedback while navigation is in progress.</span></dd></div></dl></article><article class=\"question \" id=\"us5-q5\"><span class=\"badge nonblocking-status\">Non-blocking</span> <span class=\"badge decision-status open\" aria-label=\"Open — awaiting owner confirmation\">Open</span><h4><span id=\"src-0551\" data-source=\"SRC-0551\">What happens if navigation fails?</span></h4><dl><div><dt>Decision owner / domain</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0552\" data-source=\"SRC-0552\">Product Owner / UX Designer</span></dd></div><div><dt>Temporary assumption</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0553\" data-source=\"SRC-0553\">The current selections are preserved and an actionable retry message is displayed.</span></dd></div><div><dt>Source reasoning</dt><dd><span id=\"src-0554\" data-source=\"SRC-0554\">A transient failure should not force the consumer to rebuild the search.</span></dd></div></dl></article><p class=\"muted\">If an answer changes, review the affected acceptance criteria, interaction states and tests before implementation.</p></section><section id=\"us5-states\"><h2>State transitions</h2><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Current state</th><th scope=\"col\">Consumer action</th><th scope=\"col\">Resulting state</th><th scope=\"col\">Expected visible behavior</th><th scope=\"col\">Related AC</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label=\"Current state\">No filter selected</td><td data-label=\"Consumer action\">Attempts to search</td><td data-label=\"Resulting state\">Validation state</td><td data-label=\"Expected visible behavior\">Search is not initiated and the consumer is informed that at least one criterion is required.</td><td data-label=\"Related AC\">US5 AC3</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Current state\">At least one filter selected</td><td data-label=\"Consumer action\">Selects Search Cruises</td><td data-label=\"Resulting state\">Navigation state</td><td data-label=\"Expected visible behavior\">The consumer is redirected to /cruises, where the selected criteria are displayed and applied.</td><td data-label=\"Related AC\">US5 AC1–AC5</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Current state\">Valid criteria produce no results</td><td data-label=\"Consumer action\">Results page loads</td><td data-label=\"Resulting state\">Zero-results state</td><td data-label=\"Expected visible behavior\">The selected criteria remain visible and the consumer can modify them.</td><td data-label=\"Related AC\">US5 blocking question</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The prototype simulates the search handoff. Real navigation, results and zero-results behavior remain outside its scope.</p></section><section id=\"us5-traceability\"><h2>Traceability</h2><div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">ID</th><th scope=\"col\">Source requirement</th><th scope=\"col\">Covered by</th><th scope=\"col\">Acceptance evidence</th><th scope=\"col\">Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label=\"ID\">REQ-11</td><td data-label=\"Source requirement\">Provide a Search Cruises action.</td><td data-label=\"Covered by\">US1, US5</td><td data-label=\"Acceptance evidence\">US1 AC3; US5 AC1–AC3</td><td data-label=\"Status\">Covered</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"ID\">REQ-12</td><td data-label=\"Source requirement\">Redirect to /cruises.</td><td data-label=\"Covered by\">US5</td><td data-label=\"Acceptance evidence\">US5 AC1–AC2</td><td data-label=\"Status\">Covered with minimum-selection assumption</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"ID\">REQ-13</td><td data-label=\"Source requirement\">Apply selected filters on the results page.</td><td data-label=\"Covered by\">US5</td><td data-label=\"Acceptance evidence\">US5 AC1–AC2, AC4–AC5</td><td data-label=\"Status\">Covered with assumptions</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"ID\">REQ-14</td><td data-label=\"Source requirement\">Represent the supplied default, open and completed visual states.</td><td data-label=\"Covered by\">US1–US5</td><td data-label=\"Acceptance evidence\">Story-level visual references</td><td data-label=\"Status\">Covered with design-authority assumption</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p></p></section>"};